				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				125,
				3
			],
			"Message": "style(Grove): Normalize documentation formatting and parameter spacing\n\nReflow paragraph text and reformat tables in README.md and DeepDive.md to adhere to consistent line-wrap width and proper Markdown table alignment. Add blank-line spacing around multi-line function parameters in ActivationEngine.rs for visual parameter separation.\n\n- README.md: Rewrap warning blockquote, quote, and key feature descriptions to 80-ish columns; realign all tables with properly spaced column separators and dashes; reflow Related Documentation links to break long URLs onto separate lines from their descriptions\n- DeepDive.md: Rewrap opening paragraph to standard line width\n- ActivationEngine.rs: Insert blank lines before and after the parameter block in trigger_activation, should_activate, perform_activation, and get_activation_history_for_extension for consistent multi-parameter formatting\n\nCarries forward the crate-wide style pass established in prior commits without changing any runtime behavior.",
			"SHA": "c5b7f203a2890d957a750fbd2376ce29850bf92c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T19:11:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				125,
				19
			],
			"Message": "style(Grove): Normalize import grouping and type-annotation spacing\n\nReformat crate-level and sibling imports into braced groups, strip the space after colons in type annotations, and add consistent blank lines between module declarations across the Grove crate.\n\n- **Import grouping**: Replace adjacent single-line `use crate::...` and `use super::...` imports with braced `use crate::{...}` and `use super::{...}` blocks in DiagnosticCollection, LanguageNamespace, OutputChannel, ProviderStore, VSCodeAPI, Window, Workspace, ActivationEngine, and SpineActionClient\n- **Colon spacing**: Remove the space between parameter/variable/field names and their types (`config: Self::Config` → `config:Self::Config`) across Common/Traits, Common/mod, and Library.rs\n- **Module spacing**: Insert blank lines between `pub mod` declarations in VSCode/mod, Activation/mod, and SpineActionClient/mod for consistent grouping\n- **Trailing cleanup**: Remove orphan comment lines at the end of MessageType.rs and ProtocolConfig.rs\n- **Line wrapping**: Break long function signatures across multiple lines in ActivationEngine and reformat assertion expressions in Activation/Tests\n\nConsolidates a sustained style pass that follows the crate's directory-based module convention without changing any runtime behavior.",
			"SHA": "41fe6a7c3c7a5703edcc85635c7bda21d31fda4a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:55:58Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				125,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Grove): Extract Spine protocol types into directory module\n\nMove the Spine protocol constants, message types, configuration, error types, and unit tests out of the monolithic module hierarchy into a dedicated Source/Protocol/ directory. Each type gets its own file (Constants.rs, MessageType.rs, ProtocolConfig.rs, ProtocolError.rs, Tests.rs) following the crate's directory-based module convention.\n\nThis completes the ongoing Source-level atomization of the Grove crate, reducing inline-module bloat and establishing a clear protocol layer boundary for the Spine client-server interaction model.\n\n- Constants.rs: version string, default endpoint, timeouts, buffer sizes\n- MessageType.rs: typed Heartbeat/Register/Unregister/Event/Request/Response/Error enum with u32 round-trip conversion\n- ProtocolConfig.rs: builder-pattern config struct with Default impl\n- ProtocolError.rs: thiserror-based Connection/Serialization/InvalidMessage/Timeout/Protocol errors\n- Tests.rs: coverage for config defaults, builder overrides, and message type conversion",
			"SHA": "066dc998703457cca2e7c8f220742075904213a8"
		}
	],
